soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: a restart after the standby park opens the call path again

0167 gave the restart three entry points, but a restart of a core that
the standby park (0213) had parked would have left cpu_comm shut. The
park counts one suspend and sets cpu_comm_parked_since, firmware_stop()
counted a second one, firmware_start() took one back: the count stayed
at 1, so every ioctl kept failing with -EFAULT and every kernel call
with -EBUSY, and cpu_comm_parked_since stayed set, so kernel calls would
have failed with -ENODEV behind that. The start also waited for READY
and APP_READY. APP_READY never shows on the ARM, and
mips_app_ready_assumed, which stands in for it since the boot, is
cleared by the park, so the wait would have run out its 10 s with a
firmware that had been ready after a third of a second (KD-1, L3 in the
reload plan).

Now one flag, cpu_comm_fw_down, says that the coprocessor is out of
service. The park or firmware_stop(), whichever comes first, sets it
under the call mutex and takes one count with it; a second stop, or a
stop after the park, takes none. firmware_start() clears the park and
the flag, gives that one count back, and then waits for READY alone.
Once READY is seen, app-ready is assumed again, as the boot does it.
firmware_reset() drops the assumption, because it was about the old
core. cpu_comm_call() checks the flag again inside the mutex, so a
caller that slipped past the -EBUSY test before the stop cannot reach a
core that is being halted. If the park fails, it gives the count back
only if it took one.

The wake no longer warns that the reload is missing. It says in one info
line that the restart belongs to userspace (h713-power runs
h713-mips-restart after a wake), and /proc/cpu_comm/status says "restart
pending" and whether the core is stopped.

For a restart of a running core this is the order of 0167 that ran on the
HY310 (V3, V8 of 08.10.2026): the count goes back before the wait, and
the wait ended on READY there as well, with the assumption from the boot
still set. The restart out of a real park is not measured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm.h
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm.h
@@ -538,10 +538,19 @@ extern int cpu_comm_suspend_flag;
 /*
  * Number of the suspend to RAM that parked the MIPS (cpu_comm_dev.c counts
  * them per boot), 0 while it is not parked. Set under cpu_comm_call_mutex;
- * RPCs fail with -ENODEV until a reload clears it.
+ * RPCs fail with -ENODEV until cpu_comm_firmware_start() clears it.
  */
 extern unsigned int cpu_comm_parked_since;
 
+/*
+ * The coprocessor is out of service: cpu_comm_firmware_stop() or the
+ * standby park, whichever came first, set it and took one count of
+ * cpu_comm_suspend_flag with it; cpu_comm_firmware_start() clears it and
+ * gives that count back. Under cpu_comm_call_mutex. Kernel calls fail with
+ * -EBUSY meanwhile, ioctls with -EFAULT through the count.
+ */
+extern bool cpu_comm_fw_down;
+
 /*
  * True when cpu_comm_init() found the shared region already live and chose
  * to adopt it instead of reinitialising it. Everything that writes shared
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_api.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_api.c
@@ -186,6 +186,13 @@ int cpu_comm_call(u32 comp_id, const u32 *args, unsigned int nargs,
 	/* Parked for standby: nobody answers, and a call would cost a slot. */
 	if (cpu_comm_parked_since)
 		err = -ENODEV;
+	/*
+	 * Stopped for a restart. Checked again here: a caller that passed the
+	 * test above before cpu_comm_firmware_stop() and waited for the mutex
+	 * would otherwise call a core that is being halted.
+	 */
+	else if (cpu_comm_fw_down)
+		err = -EBUSY;
 	else
 		err = cpu_comm_call_ex((int)comp_id, params, result,
 				       timeout_ms, true);
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
@@ -299,6 +299,7 @@ static struct class *cpucommclass;
 static struct proc_dir_entry *proc_dir;
 int cpu_comm_suspend_flag;
 unsigned int cpu_comm_parked_since;
+bool cpu_comm_fw_down;
 /* Suspends to RAM of this boot that reached suspend_late; not crust's cycle. */
 static unsigned int cpu_comm_s2r_count;
 
@@ -1304,9 +1305,16 @@ int cpu_comm_firmware_stop(void)
 {
 	if (!ShMemAddrBase)
 		return -ENODEV;
-	cpu_comm_suspend(0);
-	/* A call in flight finishes or times out; new ones are refused. */
+	/*
+	 * A call in flight finishes or times out; new ones are refused. One
+	 * count for the whole stop: the park took it already when it parked
+	 * the core, and a restart after a failed one finds it still taken.
+	 */
 	mutex_lock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
+	if (!cpu_comm_fw_down) {
+		cpu_comm_fw_down = true;
+		cpu_comm_suspend(0);
+	}
 	mutex_unlock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -1327,6 +1335,8 @@ int cpu_comm_firmware_reset(void)
 	memset_io((void __iomem *)(ShMemAddrBase + SHMEM_OFF_MAGIC1), 0,
 		  SHMEM_OFF_MAGIC2 + 4 - SHMEM_OFF_MAGIC1);
 	cpu_comm_shmem_adopted = false;
+	/* The boot's assumption was about the old core; start() sets it again. */
+	WRITE_ONCE(mips_app_ready_assumed, 0);
 	ret = InitCommMem(2);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
@@ -1343,8 +1353,26 @@ int cpu_comm_firmware_start(unsigned int timeout_ms)
 
 	if (!ShMemAddrBase)
 		return -ENODEV;
-	cpu_comm_resume(0);
-	while (!(isCPUReady(CPU_ID_MIPS) && isCPUAppReady(CPU_ID_MIPS))) {
+	/*
+	 * The core is released: the park is over, and the count the stop or
+	 * the park took goes back. Before the wait, as 0167 had it and as the
+	 * restarts on the HY310 ran (08.10.2026).
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
+	WRITE_ONCE(cpu_comm_parked_since, 0);
+	if (cpu_comm_fw_down) {
+		cpu_comm_fw_down = false;
+		cpu_comm_resume(0);
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
+	/*
+	 * READY, which the new firmware sets at the end of its InitCommMem.
+	 * Its APP_READY never shows on the ARM (see cpu_comm_init()), so READY
+	 * stands for both, as at boot. 0167 waited for both with the boot's
+	 * assumption still set, which made it this same wait; after a park
+	 * the assumption is gone and that loop would run out its budget.
+	 */
+	while (!isCPUReady(CPU_ID_MIPS)) {
 		if (waited >= timeout_ms) {
 			pr_err("cpu_comm: the coprocessor is not ready after %u ms (MIPS flag 0x%x)\n",
 			       waited, readl((void __iomem *)(ShMemAddrBase +
@@ -1355,8 +1383,10 @@ int cpu_comm_firmware_start(unsigned int timeout_ms)
 		msleep(10);
 		waited += 10;
 	}
-	if (!ret)
+	if (!ret) {
+		WRITE_ONCE(mips_app_ready_assumed, 1);
 		pr_info("cpu_comm: the coprocessor is ready after %u ms\n", waited);
+	}
 	blocking_notifier_call_chain(&cpu_comm_fw_chain,
 				     CPU_COMM_FIRMWARE_STARTED, &ret);
 	return ret;
@@ -1377,10 +1407,11 @@ static int cpu_comm_proc_show(struct seq_file *m, void *v)
 	seq_printf(m, "MIPS App Ready: %d\n", isCPUAppReady(CPU_ID_MIPS));
 	seq_printf(m, "Suspend: %d\n", cpu_comm_suspend_flag);
 	if (cpu_comm_parked_since)
-		seq_printf(m, "MIPS Parked: since suspend-to-RAM #%u, reload missing\n",
+		seq_printf(m, "MIPS Parked: since suspend-to-RAM #%u, restart pending\n",
 			   cpu_comm_parked_since);
 	else
 		seq_puts(m, "MIPS Parked: no\n");
+	seq_printf(m, "MIPS Stopped: %s\n", cpu_comm_fw_down ? "yes" : "no");
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -2298,6 +2329,7 @@ static int cpu_comm_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
 	void __iomem *ccu;
 	u32 rst, clk;
 	int assumed;
+	bool took;
 
 	/*
 	 * Only for standby to RAM, where the DRAM goes into self-refresh. On
@@ -2324,9 +2356,14 @@ static int cpu_comm_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
 	WRITE_ONCE(cpu_comm_parked_since, cpu_comm_s2r_count);
 	assumed = mips_app_ready_assumed;
 	mips_app_ready_assumed = 0;
+	/* A core held for a restart that failed: its stop took the count. */
+	took = !cpu_comm_fw_down;
+	if (took) {
+		cpu_comm_fw_down = true;
+		cpu_comm_suspend(0);
+	}
 	mutex_unlock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
 
-	cpu_comm_suspend(0);
 	writel(0, ccu + (H713_CCU_MIPS_RESET - H713_CCU_MIPS_CLK));
 	msleep(H713_MIPS_PARK_MS);
 	writel(0, ccu);
@@ -2343,24 +2380,33 @@ static int cpu_comm_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
 		mutex_lock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
 		WRITE_ONCE(cpu_comm_parked_since, 0);
 		mips_app_ready_assumed = assumed;
+		if (took) {
+			cpu_comm_fw_down = false;
+			cpu_comm_resume(0);
+		}
 		mutex_unlock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
-		cpu_comm_resume(0);
 		pr_err("cpu_comm: suspend-to-RAM #%u refused: park did not take (reset %08x, clock %08x), calls and ioctls open again, coprocessor state unknown\n",
 		       cpu_comm_s2r_count, rst, clk);
 		return -EIO;
 	}
-	pr_info("cpu_comm: suspend-to-RAM #%u: coprocessor parked, kernel RPCs fail with -ENODEV and ioctl RPCs with -EFAULT until it is reloaded\n",
+	pr_info("cpu_comm: suspend-to-RAM #%u: coprocessor parked, kernel RPCs fail with -ENODEV and ioctl RPCs with -EFAULT until it is restarted\n",
 		cpu_comm_s2r_count);
 	return 0;
 }
 
-/* Until the reload exists (TODO 3.3) every wake says why there is no picture. */
+/*
+ * The restart is not done here: it reads display.bin from /boot, which is
+ * frozen until the wake is through, and the receiver has to be unbound
+ * around it. h713-power runs h713-mips-restart after a wake that reports
+ * the park ("parked" in the state file of sun50i-h713-mips); every wake
+ * says it is pending.
+ */
 static int cpu_comm_resume_early(struct device *dev)
 {
 	unsigned int since = READ_ONCE(cpu_comm_parked_since);
 
 	if (since)
-		pr_warn("cpu_comm: display coprocessor parked since suspend-to-RAM #%u, reload missing (TODO 3.3)\n",
+		pr_info("cpu_comm: display coprocessor parked since suspend-to-RAM #%u, the restart is userspace's (h713-mips-restart)\n",
 			since);
 	return 0;
 }
--- a/include/linux/soc/sunxi/h713-cpu-comm.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/sunxi/h713-cpu-comm.h
@@ -234,12 +234,14 @@ bool cpu_comm_elog_full(void);
 
 /*
  * A co-processor restart (sun50i-h713-mips only): stop() refuses further
- * calls and lets one in flight finish; reset(), with the core held in reset,
- * tells the chain CPU_COMM_FIRMWARE_HALTED and rebuilds the shared region -
- * every callback descriptor goes with it, register again after the start;
- * start() accepts calls again, waits up to @timeout_ms for the new
- * firmware's ready and app-ready flags (-ETIMEDOUT), and tells the chain
- * CPU_COMM_FIRMWARE_STARTED with a pointer to that result.
+ * calls and lets one in flight finish; a core parked for standby counts as
+ * stopped, and a second stop() before the start changes nothing. reset(),
+ * with the core held in reset, tells the chain CPU_COMM_FIRMWARE_HALTED and
+ * rebuilds the shared region - every callback descriptor goes with it,
+ * register again after the start; start() ends the park, accepts calls
+ * again, waits up to @timeout_ms for the new firmware's ready flag
+ * (-ETIMEDOUT; app-ready is assumed from it, as at boot), and tells the
+ * chain CPU_COMM_FIRMWARE_STARTED with a pointer to that result.
  */
 int cpu_comm_firmware_stop(void);
 int cpu_comm_firmware_reset(void);
